      "statement_sha256": "e3ff5b35e25a6514a93d224c5203b19226b75b40d75bc92a8a94417896ba2cfb",
      "reconstructed_theorem_text": "Let Omega be any measurable space and let mu be any measure on Omega. Let H=L^2(mu;R), the real Hilbert space of almost-everywhere equivalence classes of measurable square-integrable real functions. For any bounded continuous real-linear operators A,B:H->H, if A and B are positive (symmetric with nonnegative quadratic forms) and A composed with A equals B composed with B as operators, then A=B as operators.",
      "objects": "Caller-supplied objects are the measurable space Omega, measure mu and operators A and B. No operator or root is constructed existentially. Multiplication A*A and B*B means operator composition. Positivity means symmetry together with <Au,u> >= 0 for all u, and correspondingly for B; on this complete real Hilbert space this gives selfadjointness.",
      "domains": "Omega is an arbitrary type with a measurable-space structure. mu is an arbitrary measure: neither probability, finiteness nor sigma-finiteness is an explicit assumption. H is complete and may be zero-dimensional or infinite-dimensional; it is not asserted to be finite-dimensional.",
      "quantifiers": "Universally quantify Omega, its measurable-space structure, mu, A and B. Under the three caller hypotheses A positive, B positive and equality of their squares, conclude A=B. There is no existential object and no quantification over energy certificates.",
      "assumptions": [
        "A is a bounded continuous real-linear operator on H",
        "B is a bounded continuous real-linear operator on H",
        "A.IsPositive",
        "B.IsPositive",
        "A*A=B*B"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Equality A=B of the bounded operators on the same H, so they act identically on every L2 equivalence class.",
      "scopes": "The square equality is a caller premise, not a produced certificate. The result is uniqueness among positive bounded operators with a common square. It neither constructs a square root for an arbitrary operator nor supplies a separate energy identity. It does not assert uniqueness among roots without positivity.",
      "constant_dependencies": "There are no numerical constants, asymptotic estimates, dimension caps or hidden energy/root hypotheses.",
      "nonclaims": [
        "No existence of a positive square root for arbitrary input operators",
        "No unbounded-operator statement",
        "No uniqueness for nonsymmetric or nonpositive alternatives",
        "No CFC, extension or energy premise or conclusion"
      ],
      "reconstructed_text_sha256": "59897130e2300eda5044e223549dea6131ebaf9c8c890acc933f700ab3a6592c",
      "statement_hash_recipe": "SHA256 of exact anonymous Lean statement string encoded UTF8 without BOM",
