      "statement_sha256": "684d1267ae6bc1d9957b88090ceebf172ac970384ca6c9bb7b7cd37baf1e4bd5",
      "reconstructed_theorem_text": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its normed additive-group structure and its Borel measurable-space structure, including the case dim(E)=0. Let V:E->R be C2. Let alpha,beta be nonnegative real numbers and eta a real number. Assume alpha>0, alpha<=beta, eta>0, beta*eta<=1, and, for every x,v in E, alpha*||v||^2 <= D(DV)(x)[v][v] <= beta*||v||^2. Define mu as the normalized exponential tilt of canonical volume by -V. Define J as the pushforward of mu times the standard Gaussian on E under (a,z)->(a,a+sqrt(eta) z). Define nu as the second marginal of J. Define Lambda as the pushforward of J under (a,y)->(y,2a-y). Then mu,J,nu are probability measures. There exists a Markov kernel S:E->Measure(E) such that, for every y in E, S(y) is the normalized volume tilt with log weight x->-V((y+x)/2)-||y-x||^2/(8 eta); S is a conditional kernel for Lambda, and both marginals of Lambda equal nu. For this same S there exists a bounded continuous real-linear operator T on H=L^2(nu;R) such that T is selfadjoint; for every u in H, ||Tu||<=||u||, the function representing Tu equals y->integral u(x) S(y)(dx) for nu-almost every y, and integral Tu dnu=integral u dnu. The operator D=I-(T composed with T) is positive. There exists a bounded continuous real-linear positive operator Gamma:H->H such that Gamma composed with Gamma=D and, for every u in H, ||Gamma u||^2=||u||^2-||Tu||^2. Furthermore, for every bounded continuous real-linear operator Gamma' on this same H, positivity of Gamma' and Gamma' composed with Gamma'=D imply Gamma'=Gamma.",
      "objects": "Caller-supplied: E and its displayed structures, V, alpha, beta, eta, and the displayed regularity/Hessian/step hypotheses. Locally defined: mu, J, nu and Lambda by the exact formulas in the statement. Existentially produced: a normalized Markov kernel S; a bounded real operator T acting on the actual marginal L2(nu); and a positive square-root operator Gamma on that same L2(nu). These constructions and their certificates are conclusions, not required caller witnesses.",
      "domains": "E is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space; volume is its canonical measure, and stdGaussian E is the standard Gaussian on E. V is real-valued and twice continuously Frechet differentiable on all E. alpha and beta are of type nonnegative real, coerced to real in inequalities. eta is real. H=L2(nu;R) consists of almost-everywhere classes, is complete, and need not be finite-dimensional even though E is. Every operator in the conclusion and every alternative Gamma' has precisely domain and codomain H with the same actual measure nu.",
      "quantifiers": "Universally quantify all displayed ambient data and hypotheses. The Hessian condition quantifies globally over both x and v. After the four local measure definitions, probability of mu AND probability of J AND probability of nu AND the existence of S hold together. Inside existence of S, all its kernel/disintegration/marginal claims hold AND there exists T. Inside existence of T, its operator/action/mean/defect claims hold AND there exists Gamma. Inside existence of Gamma, positivity AND exact square AND every-u energy equality AND every-Gamma' uniqueness hold together. The alternative-root quantifier is outside the preceding every-u energy quantifier; it is not indexed by u and it does not assume an energy identity for Gamma'.",
      "assumptions": [
